# Skill install groups. Three record types, whitespace separated:
#   group <id> <description>   declares a group; the description is what an
#                              installer, a plugin manifest, or a picker shows
#   explicit <id>              marks a declared group explicit: never offered by
#                              the interactive picker, excluded from --all, and
#                              installed ONLY via a literal --with <id>. When an
#                              explicit group is not selected, the installer
#                              REMOVES its previously installed artifacts —
#                              presence without recorded selection is not
#                              consent for a consent-gated group.
#   <skill> <group>            puts a skill in a declared group
# A skill with no record belongs to `core`, which always installs, and may name
# only one group. Keep LF line endings: the bash reader rejects CRLF loudly,
# the TypeScript reader trims and tolerates it — they only agree on LF.
# Adding a group is a `group` line plus its membership lines — nothing else.

group core Enforcement, planning, and workflow skills for everyday use
group product Product-model skills: evidence-backed briefs and product review
group strict-review Strict review: adversarial lane + evidence records + hard merge gate (explicit opt-in)
group review-discipline The advisory reviewer pass, as an always-loaded instruction (explicit opt-in)
explicit strict-review
explicit review-discipline

product-intelligence product
product-review product
adversarial-review strict-review
